{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:0f6f75d5647fa9f1","name":"Corellian KR-TB \"Doomtreader\"","source":{"id":"source:reference-0f6f75d5647fa9f1","title":"Corellian KR-TB \"Doomtreader\"","revision":19865,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:45:24Z","sha256":"61b79f5d02cadccb2767fe01bdc73f3137694419fa8185a68e20de95ab011474","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19865","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Corellian%20KR-TB%20%22Doomtreader%22&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-0f6f75d5647fa9f1","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["One of the Corellian Engineering Corporation's forgotten achievements is the KR-TB, better known as the Doomtreader. It represents a radical shift in design for the CEC at a time when the company is searching for a product that resonates well with the majority of their customer base. Though the YT series is nearly a century away from being realized, the KR-TB is one of the earliest attempts at designing a freighter that would be all things to all people.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["For the time, the Doomtreader's expansive cargo holds are its most lauded feature. With over 300 metric tons of capacity, a small fortune can be secured for reliable transport. The KR-TB is also designed with the solo pilot in mind. The duties of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Copilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Copilot","referenceId":"reference:49f5b0e488cfa66c"}," can be delegated to an Astromech Droid, necessitating only a small organic crew. Adequate passenger space is provided for up to six additional organics.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Next to its vast cargo capabilities, the Doomtreader is renowned for its defensive capabilities. In fact, the KR-TB earns its moniker from its heavy shields, durable construction, and Dual ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannons"},", which allow it to venture into situations that would doom lesser vessels to capture or destruction.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Even though it seems the perfect ship for the intergalactic merchant, the KR-TB is only moderately successful- in part because of the ship's high price tag. Behind the scenes, rivalries within the Corellian Engineering Corporation also play a substantial role in the model's marginalization. In the end, remaining Doomtreaders are sold at cut rates to planetary defense forces and law enforcement agencies.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The most famous KR-TB Doomtreader is ",{"tag":"i","children":["Hell's Anvil"]},". Taken as a prize by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Montross"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Montross?action=edit&redlink=1"},", a well-known Mandalorian bounty hunter and rival of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jango Fett"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jango_Fett","referenceId":"reference:bf47d6b339ff73dd"},", ",{"tag":"i","children":["Hell's Anvil"]}," is heavily modified and converted for use as a prisoner transport and mobile base. The most notorious of ",{"tag":"i","children":["Hell's Anvil's"]}," modifications is a pair of solar ionization cannons, devastating weapons that are unaffected by conventional deflector shields. With Montross's death at the hands of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jango Fett"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jango_Fett","referenceId":"reference:bf47d6b339ff73dd"},", ",{"tag":"i","children":["Hell's Anvil"]}," fades into obscurity.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Corellian KR-TB \"Doomtreader\" Statistics (CL 8)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Colossal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transport"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transport"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initi